  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "A point \\((x,y)\\) is to be chosen in the coordinate plane so that it is equally distant from the \\(x\\)-axis, the \\(y\\)-axis, and the line \\(x+y=2.\\) Then \\(x\\) is",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt2-1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\frac12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(2-\\sqrt2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "not uniquely determined"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1984-p18.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Equal distance from the axes gives \\(y=x\\) or \\(y=-x.\\) On \\(y=-x,\\) the distance to the line \\(x+y=2\\) is \\(\\sqrt2,\\) so both \\((\\sqrt2,-\\sqrt2)\\) and \\((-\\sqrt2,\\sqrt2)\\) satisfy all three distance conditions. Their \\(x\\)-coordinates differ, so \\(x\\) is not uniquely determined.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Equal distance from the two axes forces \\(|x|=|y|\\)",
        "Check both lines \\(y=x\\) and \\(y=-x\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
